# wopr's snap metadata, meta/snap.yaml in the snap. internal/tools/snapdir writes it for each
# architecture from packaging/snap/snap.yaml.in, with the version being built, and the summary and
# description from packaging/description.txt. The snap holds the release's program unchanged, so
# there is no snapcraft.yaml: snapdir prepares the directory and `snap pack` packs it
# (.github/workflows/snap.yml).
#
# base core24: the program is static and needs nothing from its base, and the empty base, bare,
# would do. But core24 is the usual base for strictly confined programs, and App Center, Firefox
# and Ubuntu's other preinstalled snaps use it, so an Ubuntu desktop already has it.
#
# Strict confinement and no plugs: wopr uses no network and reads no files. snapd's default
# AppArmor profile lets it use the terminal it runs in. Its home is ~/snap/wopr/<revision>, so
# WOPR_DEBUG's log goes to ~/snap/wopr/<revision>/.cache/wopr/debug.log. (XDG_CACHE_HOME, when the
# desktop sets it, takes the place of ~/.cache, and wopr says so if the snap may not write there.)
#
# license: snapd accepts only identifiers from its SPDX list, with no LicenseRef, so the .rpm's
# LicenseRef-Matthew-Thomas-map cannot be here. The map's terms are in NOTICE.md, which the snap
# holds.
name: wopr
version: '@VERSION@'
title: WOPR
summary: @SUMMARY@
description: |
  @DESCRIPTION@

  Open WOPR from your app grid, or type wopr in a terminal.
license: MIT AND BSD-2-Clause AND BSD-3-Clause
links:
  website:
    - https://ghostofgoes.github.io/WOPR/
  contact:
    - https://github.com/GhostofGoes/WOPR/discussions
  issues:
    - https://github.com/GhostofGoes/WOPR/issues
  source-code:
    - https://github.com/GhostofGoes/WOPR
architectures:
  - @ARCH@
base: core24
confinement: strict
grade: stable
apps:
  wopr:
    command: bin/wopr
    # The app ID, which the .deb's and the .rpm's menu entry and AppStream metadata use: software
    # centres know them as the same program.
    common-id: io.github.ghostofgoes.wopr
